course: dictionary
lesson: 15355
title: Solved: finding the answer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Mia solved the puzzle in five minutes.» Solved is the past form of solve. It means she found the answer to the puzzle. Solve is the present form, as in «I solve the puzzle», and solved tells you it has already happened.
explain: Solved can also describe something that already has an answer: «The mystery was solved, so the case was closed.» Check the meaning by swapping in «found the answer to»: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning. Context tells you which sense is used: a puzzle, a mystery or a problem.
explain: Solved is also used for problems between friends: «Tom and Sam solved their argument by taking turns.» Here it means they fixed the problem. The clues are the words argument and taking turns.
fact: «Solved» is the past form of «solve», which means to find the answer to a problem or puzzle.
fact: «Solved» can also describe something already answered, as in «a solved mystery».
fact: In maths, a problem is solved when you have found its answer.
fact: The forms of the verb are solve, solves, solving and solved.
fact: Solving a problem between friends means finding a way to fix it.
exercise: «Kai solved the maths problem before the bell.» What does solved mean? | Lost the paper it was written on | Forgot the sum completely | Broke his pencil | *Found the answer to the problem
exercise: «The mystery was solved, and the thief was caught.» Find and copy one word that tells you the answer was already found. | *solved | mystery | caught | thief
exercise: «Mia and Ben solved their argument by taking turns.» What does solved mean here? | Started a brand new argument | Wrote a poem about it | Ran away from the problem | *Fixed the problem between them
test: «The detective solved the case in one night.» Which form shows that this already happened? | solves | solving | *solved | solve
test: Which sentence uses solved to mean already answered? | I will solve the puzzle tomorrow | *The solved puzzle was pinned on the wall | She solves every puzzle fast | Solving puzzles is my favourite hobby
exam: «After hours of thinking, Sara finally solved the riddle.» What does solved tell us? | She wrote the riddle down | She gave up on the riddle | *She found the answer to the riddle | She read the riddle out loud
